# Fase 13 — spec section 49/50/52.
#
# Cloudflare Pages `_headers` syntax: a path pattern line, then indented
# "Header: value" lines applied to responses matching it. Later blocks
# override earlier ones for the same header on the same path, so the most
# specific paths are listed after the general `/*` block.
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security headers, applied to everything. Spec section 52: the app collects
# no location/contacts/microphone and camera only via explicit user action
# (avatar upload) — Permissions-Policy enforces that at the browser level,
# not just in app code. There is no CSP here: this is a Supabase-backed SPA
# talking to a project URL that is only known at deploy time (PUBLIC_
# SUPABASE_URL, injected at build time — see README section "Desplegar"),
# so a CSP tight enough to matter would either have to be templated at
# deploy time or would silently break every Supabase call; the concrete,
# static headers below are the simple option that doesn't risk that.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(self), payment=(), usb=()

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hashed build assets (src/routes/**/*.js, *.css under _app/immutable/) are
# named after their own content hash — a new deploy never reuses the old
# URL for changed content, so caching these for a year is always safe.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/_app/immutable/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The opposite case: these three are NOT hashed, and Fase 11's own service
# worker versioning (README_FASE11.md, "Estrategia de fetch") depends on the
# browser re-checking service-worker.js promptly after a deploy rather than
# serving a stale copy from an intermediate cache for hours.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/service-worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
